cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EpiFitScout, please cite it as below, together with MASTER and SAbDab."
title: "EpiFitScout: retrieval and grafting of CDR loops ranked by epitope fit"
abstract: >-
  Given a bound antibody-antigen complex and a CDR span to replace, EpiFitScout
  queries the two framework stems flanking that span against a chain database
  derived from SAbDab, returning every real loop that can bridge the gap. Each
  is grafted into the template, gated on whether its new peptide bonds are real
  bonds, rebuilt all-atom, and ranked by the interface it makes with the
  epitope. The CDR's own coordinates are never part of the query.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ashraf
    given-names: Faisal B.
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: MIT
